{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-local-constancy","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:confinement-local-constancy","kind":"proposition","title":"Local constancy of confinement level off $\\mathcal{B}$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-local-shadow-ordering","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-phase-boundary-variety"],"tags":["confinement-level","local-constancy","phase-boundary"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementLocalConstancy","text":"confinement-local-constancy.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/confinement-local-constancy.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:confinement-local-constancy\"></a><p><em>The <a href=\"#def:confinement-level\">confinement level</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell(K, q)</code> is <strong>locally constant</strong> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Q \\setminus \\mathcal{B}</code>. For any <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\notin \\mathcal{B}</code>, there exists an open <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\ni q</code> such that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell(K, q') = \\ell(K, q)</code> for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q' \\in U</code>. The level changes only at points of the <a href=\"#prop:phase-boundary-variety\">phase-boundary variety</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}</code> — these correspond exactly to the <strong>categorical phase boundaries</strong>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/confinement-local-constancy.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"12.4.9"}
